    "claim": "The peer proxy cannot stream InputStream command results: peer.local (newbound_core) creates a peer stream (begin_stream/write_stream pump) ONLY for `file` responses - a bytes `body` (an InputStream return like camera live) is a process-local DataBytes ref that cannot cross the wire, so the viewer-side peer.remote finds neither stream_id nor usable body and returns its 404 sentinel. Symptom: remote live view falls back to JPEG polling instantly (File-returning commands - snapshot, last_keyframe, play - stream fine over peers, which is why everything else works in the HUD). Fix sketch (platform, owner blessing required per the boundary doctrine): a third branch in peer.local mirroring the file branch - when body is bytes, begin_stream and pump DataBytes.read into write_stream until close, carrying the mime type; peer.remote already join_streams. Found 2026-08-12 diagnosing the owner HUD report.",
