    "claim": "InputStream-over-peers landed on newbound branch claude/peer-stream-bytes-bodies (2026-08-12, standalone off master, awaiting owner review): peer.peer.local gained a bytes-body branch (begin_stream + DataBytes pump, 16KB chunks, mime carried, 30s starvation cap) and peer.service.listen gained the s_4 close-back - s_2 detects a dead local reader (write false / entry gone) and answers s_4, whose handler retires the matching STREAMWRITERS entry so the senders write_stream fails and its pump stops ~1s after viewer disconnect. Wire-compatible with old peers in both directions. Two-instance lab verification: same-host peering works via discovery master/slave + setuser with keepalive (maintenance auto-connects; peer users must be in a group check_security accepts - production uses admin; a non-admin group 404s every proxied command instantly, which is also the diagnostic signature of an unauthorized peer). Remote status/file/live all green; live delivers ffprobe-clean fMP4 into an in-page Chromium fetch with correct avc1 codec parse. CRITICAL build gotcha: dev.code patches on a STATIC library regenerate src and build the rlib but do NOT relink the host binary - test runs silently exercise the old code until a cargo build relinks (~2s); check strings <binary> for a new literal before trusting a static-lib test.",
